<Base lang="en" title="Writing"><article class="prose"><p class="label">Writing</p><h1>The words arrive before the biography.</h1><p>Fiction, essays, and fragments that need not justify themselves at once live here. Chinese is the natural home of the originals; English pages carry context and a small number of carefully selected translations — not hurried machine versions of every piece.</p><div class="grid"><section class="card"><div><span class="number">ESSAYS</span><h3>100 Small Things About Toronto</h3><p>A published essay collection: one hundred small entries plus a set of Montreal notes, written with no outline — the recurring threads only became visible in hindsight.</p><p class="essay-more"><a href="/en/writing/toronto-100/">Read more →</a></p></div></section><section class="card"><div><span class="number">FANFICTION</span><h3>Fan fiction</h3><p>Mostly Genshin Impact, centered on one pairing across roughly thirty pieces, plus a handful of short pieces for other works. Someone else's story, carrying my own real thinking underneath.</p><p class="essay-more"><a href="/en/writing/fanfiction/">Read more →</a></p></div></section><section class="card"><div><span class="number">NOVEL</span><h3>Our Insync</h3><p>An original semi-autobiographical novel, twenty chapters — a fictional frame carrying a real piece of my own childhood.</p><p class="essay-more"><a href="/en/writing/our-insync/">Read more →</a></p></div></section><section class="card"><div><span class="number">MUSINGS</span><h3>Musings</h3><p>Loose, occasional writing that doesn't belong to any collection yet. Content coming soon.</p></div></section></div><aside class="note">Private files and unselected drafts are never synced here, and nothing is published without being cleared first.</aside></article></Base>

